infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Theming runtime: cascade vs JS context
  desc Flip data-theme → zero re-render. JS context → every consumer re-renders.
  compares
    - label CSS custom properties
      children
        - label Zero re-render on switch
          desc Flip data-theme; the browser recomputes styles, no React state changed
        - label SSR-safe, crosses frameworks
          desc Inline script sets the attribute pre-paint; works across micro-frontends
        - label Cost — untyped strings
          desc Generate TS declarations; JS reads need getComputedStyle
    - label JS theme objects
      children
        - label Typed, composable values
          desc First-class in the language via ThemeProvider context
        - label Cost — re-renders every consumer
          desc A switch changes the context value — ~1,800 components re-render
        - label Cost — framework-locked
          desc Tokens tied to React; the cascade could have swapped them free
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
